zufast is licensed under the MIT licence (see LICENSE and LICENSE.md).

It bundles, under inst/include/zufast/vendor/, code from three upstream
libraries, each under its own licence, and a state table transcribed into
inst/include/zufast/utf8.h:

  ffc.h    (C port of fast_float)   MIT            licenses/ffc-LICENSE
  Ryu      (d2s, f2s)               Boost-1.0      licenses/ryu-LICENSE
  xxHash   (xxhash.h only)          BSD-2-Clause   licenses/xxhash-LICENSE
  Hoehrmann's UTF-8 DFA table       MIT            notice in utf8.h

The licence texts are installed with the package under licenses/. Because
zufast is header-only, every package that uses `LinkingTo: zufast` compiles
this code into its own shared object, which is a redistribution these
licences permit with their notices kept. inst/COPYRIGHTS gives the copyright
holders, the pinned upstream commits and the patches applied;
tools/vendor/manifest.tsv and tools/patches/ in the source repository,
https://github.com/pedrobtz/zufast, record the same, with checksums.
